# CVF EARTR-ESC-R0 Source Collaboration Enrichment Design Decision

Memory class: FULL_RECORD

Status: REVISED_PENDING_RB01_CLOSURE_CONFIRMATION

docType: design_decision

authorityStatus: NON_AUTHORITATIVE_UNTIL_RB01_CLOSURE_AND_OPERATOR_DISPOSITION

Date: 2026-08-29

External knowledge intake routing: REQUIRED

## Purpose

Define the smallest design-only enrichment needed to make the recurring
Operator, External Agent, Local Agent, and governed CVF implementation
collaboration deterministic before future source-repository intake begins.

This packet evaluates an operator-transmitted External Agent proposal. It does
not absorb a selected source repository, change protocol code, revise a schema,
refresh a distributed packet, authorize implementation, or open a new owner.

## Scope / Methodology

- read the current round-trip representation contract, generator/validator,
  focused tests, public compact projection, and portable return contract;
- route the operator-transmitted proposal through the current external-agent
  finding workflow and knowledge-intake chain map;
- compare each proposed artifact, role, state, and authority transition against
  `CVF_EXTERNAL_ABSORPTION_CORE_STANDARD.md` and KIOD owner surfaces;
- actively attempt to prove that no new protocol, profile, registry, runtime,
  state machine, truth owner, receipt owner, or authority owner is needed;
- preserve only source-backed, bounded existing-owner enrichment candidates;
- leave implementation and representation refresh closed.

## Findings / Position

The proposed collaboration sequence is substantially already implemented as
governed protocol semantics. The current `SOURCE_PACK_PREPARATION` mode,
structured external return, chain map, finding workflow, Core Standard, KIOD
owner/overlap route, Operator gate, and later Work Order chain cover the full
flow. External adversarial review confirmed the existing-owner route and found
three bounded corrections: the candidate collection needs a discriminated
two-lane contract, Local reconciliation needs immutable parent-return binding,
and strict items need an explicit version discriminator plus dual-reader
behavior. These corrections justify a protocol minor enrichment, not a new
collaboration structure.

